1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,700
(EP09 Behind-the-Scenes)

2
00:00:02,740 --> 00:00:05,980
(Behind-the-Scenes 1)

3
00:00:06,060 --> 00:00:07,970
(Behind-the-Scenes)

4
00:00:07,970 --> 00:00:10,660
I didn't dream at all last night.

5
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:14,830
You went straight to sleep?

6
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:16,260
Yeah, I was out.

7
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:22,350
And I woke up on my own.

8
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:25,870
Then you came down?

9
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:28,230
Maybe

10
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:31,230
something told me

11
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:33,750
to get up and find you.

12
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:37,950
I slept in my clothes and shoes.

13
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:40,550
So I could just wake up,

14
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:41,750
get up, and go.

15
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:43,470
That's not good.

16
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,390
I should've waited

17
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:47,470
until you took off your shoes
and got in bed.

18
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:53,300
(Teasing)

19
00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:09,020
(Behind-the-Scenes 2)

20
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:10,740
(Behind-the-Scenes)

21
00:01:10,760 --> 00:01:13,400
Do you watch TV at home?

22
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:15,230
Not much.

23
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,830
It's no fun watching alone.

24
00:01:19,360 --> 00:01:21,430
What do you usually watch?

25
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:23,350
Movies sometimes.

26
00:01:23,440 --> 00:01:25,630
What kind of movies?

27
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:27,780
Comedies when I'm down.

28
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:29,990
Comedies?

29
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:33,590
Do you ever go to the movies alone?

30
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:35,550
I've only done it...

31
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:38,270
once in my life.

32
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:41,630
I had nowhere to go,

33
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:43,950
so I went to see a movie.

34
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:45,740
Yeah.

35
00:01:46,480 --> 00:01:48,150
There's a theater in Beijing

36
00:01:48,160 --> 00:01:49,910
with a main screen

37
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:51,830
and projections on both sides.

38
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:53,670
Projections on both sides?

39
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:54,870
Yeah, on both sides.

40
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:56,390
It kind of wraps around you.

41
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:57,910
The main screen is in front,

42
00:01:57,920 --> 00:01:59,510
with projections

43
00:01:59,520 --> 00:02:01,550
on both side walls?

44
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:03,630
So you watch it like this?

45
00:02:09,030 --> 00:02:09,670
No.

46
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:12,830
I don't get it.

47
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:15,870
So the movie plays on all the walls?

48
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:18,910
I'll take you there sometime.

49
00:02:18,910 --> 00:02:19,450
Okay.

50
00:02:24,020 --> 00:02:28,940
(Behind-the-Scenes 3)

51
00:02:28,980 --> 00:02:33,020
(Behind-the-Scenes)

52
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:34,300
(Eye contact)

53
00:02:40,420 --> 00:02:41,900
(Squeezes)

54
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:44,590
Guess which one is the middle finger.

55
00:02:45,890 --> 00:02:46,410
This one.

56
00:02:49,340 --> 00:02:50,180
(Picks the ring finger)

57
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:54,370
Wrong.

58
00:02:55,090 --> 00:02:56,390
You hid it, right?

59
00:02:56,480 --> 00:02:57,710
No, it's right here.

60
00:02:57,720 --> 00:02:58,500
Really?

61
00:02:58,500 --> 00:02:59,220
(Tries)

62
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:01,220
(Looks away)

63
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:03,830
Okay, which one's the middle finger?

64
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:07,330
This one.

65
00:03:11,040 --> 00:03:13,230
No! You hid it!

66
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:15,430
No wonder. One's missing.

67
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:17,230
There are only three fingers.

68
00:03:18,770 --> 00:03:19,390
My turn.

69
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:22,230
Don't look.

70
00:03:23,260 --> 00:03:24,620
(Looks away)

71
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:27,230
Ready?

72
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:28,030
Not yet.

73
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:29,940
(Focused)

74
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:31,710
Now, guess.

75
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:42,180
Three, two, one.

76
00:03:44,920 --> 00:03:46,310
(Picks the ring finger again)
You always pick that one.

77
00:03:46,320 --> 00:03:46,990
Yeah, why?

78
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:51,150
Because of love.

79
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:53,200
Because of love.

80
00:04:01,420 --> 00:04:06,340
(Behind-the-Scenes 4)

81
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:08,190
(Behind-the-Scenes)
We need to change, right?

82
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:12,110
(Complimenting)
You look beautiful today.

83
00:04:12,880 --> 00:04:13,860
I always do.

84
00:04:14,390 --> 00:04:15,600
(Imitating)
I always do.

85
00:04:22,520 --> 00:04:23,670
Do I look like you?

86
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:25,030
Lips slightly parted,

87
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:26,110
head tilted,

88
00:04:27,760 --> 00:04:29,030
and a shy

89
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:31,030
yet confident look.

90
00:04:35,890 --> 00:04:37,110
You're so cheesy!

91
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:38,030
That's you.

92
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:41,830
I'm copying you.

93
00:04:43,880 --> 00:04:44,670
Let's go.

94
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:46,430
Pick a helmet.

95
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:48,320
This one's cute.

96
00:04:48,320 --> 00:04:49,050
Try this one.

97
00:04:49,050 --> 00:04:49,540
Okay.

98
00:04:54,860 --> 00:04:55,540
(Can't buckle it)

99
00:04:58,400 --> 00:04:59,750
Let me help you.

100
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:01,790
Thanks.

101
00:05:06,910 --> 00:05:07,350
Don't laugh.

102
00:05:14,030 --> 00:05:14,670
Thanks.

103
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:15,790
Sure.

104
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:16,950
Let's go.

105
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:19,310
Can you tighten this?

106
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:22,710
Your head's too small.

107
00:05:23,010 --> 00:05:23,610
Yeah.

108
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:34,270
How's that? Okay?

109
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:36,990
Let's go.

110
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:37,620
Okay, let's go.

111
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:44,300
(Behind-the-Scenes 5)

112
00:05:44,840 --> 00:05:46,510
(Behind-the-Scenes)
Sunrise or sunset?

113
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:48,670
Probably sunset.

114
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:50,350
Sunset?

115
00:05:50,840 --> 00:05:51,390
When the five of us

116
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:52,950
went on that group date,

117
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:55,430
the sunset was beautiful.

118
00:05:55,760 --> 00:05:57,630
We were all talking,

119
00:05:57,760 --> 00:05:59,190
and I said I loved sunsets.

120
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:02,350
Why do you like sunsets?

121
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:05,590
Did you know
there's a 20-minute blue hour

122
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:06,310
after sunset?

123
00:06:06,310 --> 00:06:06,930
Yeah.

124
00:06:07,080 --> 00:06:08,350
Once the sun sets,

125
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:09,230
it feels like I can finally relax.

126
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:09,710
Yeah.

127
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:12,750
How about rainy days?

128
00:06:13,760 --> 00:06:14,790
I like them.

129
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:15,910
You do?

130
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:17,630
Depends on my mood.

131
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:23,110
If I'm sharing an umbrella

132
00:06:23,110 --> 00:06:24,340
in the drizzle

133
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:25,400
with someone I like,

134
00:06:25,400 --> 00:06:26,260
I'd be

135
00:06:26,590 --> 00:06:27,280
really happy.

136
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:30,310
But if I'm already having a bad day

137
00:06:30,320 --> 00:06:31,550
and it rains,

138
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:33,390
I'd feel incredibly unlucky.

139
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:36,190
Like when you came, it poured.

140
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:37,910
Yeah, it even hailed.

141
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:39,590
Then it started pouring.

142
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:41,230
It was crazy.

143
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:43,430
Hail in June?
How could that even happen?

144
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:46,350
Maybe the universe knew
I was coming to see you

145
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:48,350
and threw a few tests

146
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:49,670
my way.

147
00:06:51,520 --> 00:06:52,750
I thought so too.

148
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:55,310
To see how serious I was.

149
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:57,750
Then, right after I called you,

150
00:06:58,440 --> 00:06:59,470
the universe must've realized

151
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:01,350
I was serious

152
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:02,870
and finally let me through.

153
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:08,030
So you're an angel.

154
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:09,190
You're an angel.

155
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:11,750
You can talk to the universe.

156
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:23,220
(Behind-the-Scenes 6)

157
00:07:23,300 --> 00:07:24,820
(Behind-the-Scenes)
(Looking at Polaroids)

158
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:25,670
I'll show you one

159
00:07:25,680 --> 00:07:27,190
you might not remember.

160
00:07:30,460 --> 00:07:32,100
(Looks closely)

161
00:07:33,440 --> 00:07:34,800
What did we do that day?

162
00:07:35,650 --> 00:07:37,280
We made...

163
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:40,390
cumin pork, right?

164
00:07:41,130 --> 00:07:41,510
Right?

165
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:42,630
And then?

166
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,670
Or did we make salmon that day?
Wait.

167
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:48,430
No, it was cumin pork.

168
00:07:50,240 --> 00:07:51,590
Okay, I'll tell you.

169
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:52,830
We went boating that day.

170
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:53,750
Remember now?

171
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:55,470
This one?

172
00:07:58,340 --> 00:07:58,950
Yeah, it is.

173
00:07:59,830 --> 00:08:00,520
You sure?

174
00:08:00,520 --> 00:08:00,950
Wait, no.

175
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:03,470
Yeah, that's the day.

176
00:08:05,290 --> 00:08:05,760
Wow.

177
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:07,590
Then what day was this?

178
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:12,270
The day we made breakfast.

179
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:13,870
What did we eat?

180
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:18,180
We had that green toast.

181
00:08:19,510 --> 00:08:21,130
Green toast?

182
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:22,650
(Teasing)
Are you sure?

183
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:24,350
(Seriously)
Yeah, the matcha one.

184
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:25,540
You sure?

185
00:08:25,720 --> 00:08:26,800
(Pressing)
What if you're wrong?

186
00:08:28,320 --> 00:08:29,630
(Certain)
I'm sure.

187
00:08:31,840 --> 00:08:32,630
Right?

188
00:08:35,900 --> 00:08:40,820
(Behind-the-Scenes 7)

189
00:08:40,860 --> 00:08:41,580
(Behind-the-Scenes)

190
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:42,870
Let's get everyone a gift.

191
00:08:43,010 --> 00:08:43,900
Yeah.

192
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:46,230
Should we...

193
00:08:46,280 --> 00:08:46,950
Choose for them?

194
00:08:47,640 --> 00:08:49,750
Orange, white, and black?

195
00:08:51,220 --> 00:08:51,850
Let's see.

196
00:08:56,120 --> 00:08:57,590
How about the guys...

197
00:08:58,700 --> 00:08:59,210
get these?

198
00:08:59,210 --> 00:08:59,910
(Punching bags)
Sure.

199
00:09:00,280 --> 00:09:01,670
And gloves for the girls?

200
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:05,190
Nice.

201
00:09:05,190 --> 00:09:05,560
Good?

202
00:09:05,560 --> 00:09:06,320
Yeah.

203
00:09:09,280 --> 00:09:10,350
(Before bed)
All right, guys.

204
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:11,670
Gifts first.

205
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:13,870
These are for the guys.

206
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:16,030
We did Muay Thai today.

207
00:09:16,030 --> 00:09:17,060
Whoa!

208
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:18,580
Thanks.

209
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:20,510
Each guy gets

210
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:22,150
a punching bag.

211
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,710
Take your stress out on it.

212
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:27,550
And...

213
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:29,270
gloves for the girls.

214
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:31,510
So we get hit?

215
00:09:32,040 --> 00:09:32,630
Yeah.

216
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:33,110
Now I get it.

217
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:38,470
We got these for you.

218
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:40,950
We tried boxing today.

219
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:41,390
Boxing?

220
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:42,310
Thanks.

221
00:09:43,400 --> 00:09:44,670
Punching bags for the guys

222
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:47,110
and gloves for the girls.

223
00:09:48,080 --> 00:09:48,800
KO!

224
00:09:50,820 --> 00:09:55,740
(Behind-the-Scenes 8)

225
00:09:56,520 --> 00:09:57,950
(Behind-the-Scenes)
I remember you told me before

226
00:09:57,960 --> 00:09:59,670
that you take after your dad more.

227
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:02,390
But my mom and dad

228
00:10:02,400 --> 00:10:03,950
(Big eyes)
both have eyes like this.

229
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:05,350
Just like yours.

230
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:08,260
(Stares)

231
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:10,150
Have you ever heard this saying?

232
00:10:10,160 --> 00:10:12,670
They say when a couple's
been together for a long time,

233
00:10:12,680 --> 00:10:15,430
they start looking like each other.

234
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:16,630
Have you heard that before?

235
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,790
When you're
around someone long enough,

236
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:21,670
you notice all their little expressions.

237
00:10:21,680 --> 00:10:22,900
The other person sees them

238
00:10:22,900 --> 00:10:23,470
and picks them up.

239
00:10:23,980 --> 00:10:24,350
Yeah.

240
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:25,990
So your little expressions
become more alike.

241
00:10:25,990 --> 00:10:26,430
Yeah.

242
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:28,750
Then I feel like

243
00:10:28,760 --> 00:10:30,990
if someone spent enough time with you,

244
00:10:30,990 --> 00:10:32,510
they might become...

245
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:36,110
gentler.

246
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:41,510
Are you usually a pretty gentle person?

247
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:43,350
I'm usually pretty quiet.

248
00:10:45,220 --> 00:10:46,820
So you're more
of the cool, distant type?

249
00:10:47,040 --> 00:10:48,430
I'm not trying to act distant.

250
00:10:48,680 --> 00:10:50,590
I'm honestly just introverted

251
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:51,630
and not great at expressing myself.

252
00:10:53,360 --> 00:10:54,990
With my

253
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,630
friends and the guys,

254
00:10:56,720 --> 00:10:57,830
I can still talk.

255
00:10:57,830 --> 00:10:59,220
At least I can hold a conversation.

256
00:10:59,760 --> 00:11:01,630
But with girls, I

257
00:11:01,640 --> 00:11:04,030
sometimes don't know what to say.

258
00:11:04,120 --> 00:11:04,950
I'm bad with words.

259
00:11:05,520 --> 00:11:06,050
I don't think so.

260
00:11:06,330 --> 00:11:07,010
No?

261
00:11:11,740 --> 00:11:16,700
(Behind-the-Scenes 9)

262
00:11:16,780 --> 00:11:18,380
(Behind-the-Scenes)

263
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:19,920
I really didn't expect you and me

264
00:11:19,920 --> 00:11:21,250
to be the same lover type.

265
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:23,030
Did you expect us to be the same?

266
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:24,840
No.

267
00:11:26,480 --> 00:11:27,860
Yiheng, how do you think our Kite styles

268
00:11:27,880 --> 00:11:28,670
are different?

269
00:11:28,850 --> 00:11:30,150
Our Kite styles?

270
00:11:30,150 --> 00:11:30,940
(Thinking)

271
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:33,230
I think we're basically the same.

272
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:35,350
The biggest difference
is how we socialize.

273
00:11:35,360 --> 00:11:36,590
I'm more introverted,

274
00:11:36,590 --> 00:11:37,640
and you're more outgoing.

275
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:39,670
But I think both of us

276
00:11:39,800 --> 00:11:43,230
tend to be the kind of people

277
00:11:43,240 --> 00:11:45,430
who give our partners space.

278
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:47,670
Xiaoyu is also a Sunny Lover.

279
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:48,670
I'm a Sunny Lover.

280
00:11:50,160 --> 00:11:52,110
How do you think your Sun style differs

281
00:11:52,120 --> 00:11:53,310
from Kaiyi's?

282
00:11:53,940 --> 00:11:55,830
I feel like Kaiyi
doesn't just take care of everyone.

283
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:57,390
Especially with you,

284
00:11:57,400 --> 00:11:59,790
the chemistry between you two

285
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:01,810
is really great.

286
00:12:01,810 --> 00:12:03,980
Yeah, so it kind of feels like

287
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,740
(Personal fireplace)
she's your own personal fireplace.

288
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:17,860
(Behind-the-Scenes 10)

289
00:12:17,940 --> 00:12:19,820
(Behind-the-Scenes)

290
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:22,390
We're usually pretty polite
with each other.

291
00:12:23,040 --> 00:12:23,990
Pretty polite.

292
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:26,510
I'm alright.

